Description: Build the Windows installer without RLZ. The ungoogled-chromium
 patch 0021-disable-rlz turns off enable_rlz_support, which removes the //rlz
 library targets, but the Windows setup.exe still depended on
 //rlz:rlz_lib_no_network to clear RLZ state on uninstall, and the rlz_id
 example tool still depended on //rlz:rlz_lib, so gn gen failed on Windows.
 Brumel never writes RLZ state, so the uninstall step is removed and rlz_id is
 built only when RLZ support is on.
Origin: brumel
Module: fixes
Feature: CORE-006
Upstreamable: no
SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
